ledger=json.loads((V/'VERIFICATION.txt').read_text(encoding='utf8'));ledger.setdefault('supplemental',{})['polish32']={'goals':'tight metric icon/count spacing; cancellable async HTTP transfers; non-collapsing category lane and untransformed mobile panel; bare ASCII/Chinese-IDN description links; explicit toolbar background/shadow reset; no early client autoplay and no BTR zero-position override','behaviors':behavior,'rollbacks':rollbacks,'cumulative_diff_reconstructs_all_five_files':True,'unit_output':(V/'polish32-unit.txt').read_text(encoding='utf8',errors='replace'),'build_output':(V/'polish32-build.txt').read_text(encoding='utf8',errors='replace'),'limitations':'122 unit tests. Async WinHTTP normal transfer and cancellation during body, pending headers and immediately before startup executed in dedicated test harness; canceled tasks complete under1500ms, preserve sentinel destination and remove all task partials. Never close a synchronous WinHTTP request from another thread; request owner cancels its async request and waits for HANDLE_CLOSING callback before freeing context. Runtime verified first category link hit-test in 20 route/control/width combinations (home/video, traffic/windows,480/800/1050/1280/1920), theme light/dark/light toolbar with hostile background image and local black variable, metric icon/count gap4 and group gap8. Bare-domain fixtures preserve surrounding prose/emoji and use punycode href for genuine Chinese IDN. No outgoing request made to user example domains. Resume tested with delayed official-player fixture and BTR pure guard matrix; private actual Bili account history not read. Initial old autoplay/theme tests expected superseded behavior and were rewritten to stronger delayed-resume/background-image contracts. Initial runtime metric probe had an unmatched closure; fixed only test expression. Cancellation current-renderer control is shown after native start, not during URL parse/save dialog. No new system clipboard writes this turn. BTR rollback uses baseline sibling and cumulative patch adds fifth BTR source input.' ,'runtime_reports':['polish32-runtime.json','polish32-native.json'],'native_test_output':(V/'polish32-native.txt').read_text(encoding='utf8',errors='replace'),'patch_input_files':['blocker.original.user.js','ui-v0.1.0/enhance.original.js','ui-v0.1.0/main.original.cpp','ui-v0.1.4/bridge.original.js','polish32-baseline/btr.user.js'],'support_files':{str(p):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in [R/'CMakeLists.txt',R/'scripts/build.ps1',R/'README.md',R/'vendor/plugins.lock.json']}};(V/'VERIFICATION.txt').write_text(json.dumps(ledger,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf8')
